List a directory, or stat a single file, in the in-world filesystem.

usage: @fls [path]

With no argument, lists the VFS root. With a directory path, lists its
entries; a directory is shown with a trailing '/'. With a file path, shows
that one file's size. Each line is "<kind> <size> <name>", where kind is
'd' for a directory or '-' for a file, and a directory's size is shown as
'-'.

The path must be absolute, for example /src. Wizard only.

Example:
  @fls /src
      List the sources under /src.

See also @fcat, @ftype, @fedit, @fget.
